.policy "drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field" revision 1
.description "Keep secret model fields such as passwords, secret keys and API tokens out of a DRF ModelSerializer's output, or make them write-only."
.language python
.mode log
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. A ModelSerializer returns every field its Meta lets in: all of them with
// `fields = "__all__"`, every one `exclude` does not name, or the ones `fields` lists. When one of them holds a
// secret (a password or its hash, an API key, a token, a client or signing secret, a private key, an OTP seed,
// stored credentials), the serializer's output carries it (OWASP API3, "Broken Object Property Level
// Authorization"). The rule resolves the serializer's Meta.model to a model of the run in any module (lib/drf's
// drf_cls_q: through the project's import root and package re-exports too), reads its fields, own and inherited from
// the run's model bases (an abstract base in a third module), and reports, at the Meta value that lets the field in:
//   - `fields = "__all__"`, or an `exclude` that does not name the field: at that value, once per secret field;
//   - `fields` listing the field: at the listed string (lists joined with `+`, `Base.Meta.fields`, and a module
//     constant `fields = BUCKET_FIELDS` included; a string outside any class is reported at the Meta value);
//   - a SerializerMethodField in the output whose method returns `obj.<secret field>`: at the field.
// A field is a secret when its name says so and its class can hold one. Detection is by name, the one thing a
// secret column has in common, so the rule stays in log. Names (the whole name):
// `[*_]password[s][_hash]` (`passwd`, `passphrase`), `[*_]secret[s][_key|_access_key|_token|_value]`,
// `[*_]token[_key|_secret|_value]`, `[*_]tokens_(key|secret|value)`, `[*_](api|secret|private|signing|encryption)[_]key[s]`,
// `[*_](otp|totp|hotp)[_secret|_seed|_key]`, `[*_](mfa|2fa)_(secret|seed|key)`, `[*_]credential[s]`. The plural
// `tokens` alone (NLP tokens, stored LLM token counts) and `access_key` without `secret` (an object-storage key id,
// whose secret is `secret_access_key`) name non-secrets more often than secrets and are not on the list. Classes
// that cannot hold one are left out: booleans, numbers, dates and times, durations, auto keys, relations (a relation
// returns the related row's key). A field class the run defines (`EncryptedTextField`) or imports from another
// package counts when it is called `…Field`. A model deriving from Django's AbstractBaseUser, AbstractUser or User
// (Django's `User`, `get_user_model()`, or a module's `User = get_user_model()`) has `password`, Django's hash.
//   class ApiClient(CredentialModel): ...              # core/models.py: CredentialModel has api_token
//   class ApiClientSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):
//       class Meta:
//           model = ApiClient
//           exclude = ["owner"]                        reported: api_token goes out
//   class UserCreateSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):
//       class Meta:
//           model = User
//           fields = ["id", "username", "password"]
//           extra_kwargs = {"password": {"write_only": True}}         not reported
// It leaves alone a field the serializer hides: declared (by the serializer or a run base it inherits the name from)
// as `x = None`, as a field with `write_only=True`, a HiddenField or SerializerMethodField, a field reading another
// `source=`, or a field class that is not rest_framework's own (a project's ObfuscatedPasswordField); with no
// declaration, `Meta.extra_kwargs` giving it `write_only: True` (lib/drf's drf_extra_kw_q: a literal, `dict(...)` or
// a module constant); and a serializer with a `to_representation` (its own or a run base's) whose class body, or a
// run base's, holds the field's name as a string outside its Meta (`data.pop("password")`, or a
// `secure_fields = ["password"]` list the method pops). Also left alone: secret-looking names that are not secrets
// by class or name (`password_changed_at`, `token_expires`, `has_password`, `tokens_used`, `tokens`, `access_key`, a
// BooleanField `secret_santa`), plain Serializers, serializers whose model is outside the run (other than Django's
// users), and test code.
// Gaps: a declared plain field next to `extra_kwargs` write_only is reported (DRF ignores extra_kwargs for declared
// fields, so it is exposed); a secret under a name the list misses (`key`, `pin`, `salt`) is not reported; tokens
// meant to be shown are reported, since no name separates them: a token returned once by the endpoint that creates
// it, an invite or share-link token, a device's pairing token; a serializer only ever used to validate input (never
// rendered) is reported; a plain Serializer declaring `secret_access_key = CharField()` is not; `fields` built by a
// call or a comprehension is not read; a to_representation that pops the field without naming it in the class (a
// helper in another module) is reported.

#include "lib/drf.rerail"

// A serializer, its model and their bases may sit in different modules: each is judged by symbol (sx_out, sx_hidden,
// sx_method_out), and a finding is written at the node of the file that holds the Meta value, the listed string or
// the declaration (drf_hv, sx_str_spot), which need not be the serializer's own.
.violation SerializerExposesSecret(at: node, ser: symbol, model: symbol, x: symbol, how: symbol) "`{ser}` puts `{model}.{x}`, a secret, in its output ({how}). Drop it from the output or make it write-only, unless this serializer shows a token once to its creator."
SerializerExposesSecret(at, s, m, x, how) :- sx_out(c, mq, x, how, h, ""), !sx_hidden(c, x), drf_hv(h, at),
    split_dot(c, _, s), sx_model_label(mq, m).
SerializerExposesSecret(at, s, m, x, how) :- sx_out(c, mq, x, how, _, w), w != "", !sx_hidden(c, x),
    sx_str_spot(at, w, x), split_dot(c, _, s), sx_model_label(mq, m).
SerializerExposesSecret(at, s, m, x, "a SerializerMethodField returns it") :- sx_method_out(c, mq, x, hd),
    drf_hv(hd, v), unparen(v, at), split_dot(c, _, s), sx_model_label(mq, m).

// sx_model_label(mq, m): the model's name for the message: its class name, or `User` for get_user_model().
.decl sx_model_label(mq: symbol, m: symbol)
sx_model_label(mq, m) :- sx_ser(_, mq), mq != "get_user_model()", split_dot(mq, _, m).
sx_model_label("get_user_model()", "User").

// ---- serializers and their models --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Bases are followed through lib/drf's drf_anc (drf_cls_q: the project's import root, package re-exports), model
// bases and serializer bases alike.
// sx_ms(c): c is a ModelSerializer: lib/drf's drf_model_serializer_q, or a class with one among its run bases.
.decl sx_ms(c: symbol)
sx_ms(c) :- drf_model_serializer_q(c).
sx_ms(c) :- drf_anc(c, b), drf_model_serializer_q(b).
// sx_opt(c, k, h): ModelSerializer c's Meta option k is home h: lib/drf's drf_opt, else (a serializer lib/drf does
// not see) the option of the `class Meta` in c's own body.
.decl sx_opt(c: symbol, k: symbol, h: symbol)
sx_opt(c, k, h) :- sx_ms(c), drf_opt(c, k, h).
sx_opt(c, k, h) :- sx_ms(c), !drf_node_q(c), drf_qmeta(c, mq), drf_qattr(mq, k), h = @dot(mq, k).

// sx_ser(c, mq): c is a ModelSerializer outside test code whose Meta.model is mq: a qualified class name, or
// "get_user_model()" for `model = get_user_model()`.
.decl sx_ser(c: symbol, mq: symbol)
sx_ser(c, mq) :- sx_opt(c, "model", h), drf_hsym(h, mq), !drf_qtest(c).
sx_ser(c, "get_user_model()") :- sx_opt(c, "model", h), sx_gum_home(h), !drf_qtest(c).
// sx_gum_home(h): home h's value is `get_user_model()`, or (`UserModel = get_user_model()` in its module, then
// `model = UserModel`) a name bound to it.
.decl sx_gum_home(h: symbol)
sx_gum_home(h) :- drf_hv(h, v), unparen(v, u), sx_gum_call(u).
sx_gum_home(h) :- drf_hv(h, v), unparen(v, u), kind(u, "identifier"), look(u, x, s), asg(s, x, r, _), unparen(r, g),
    sx_gum_call(g).
.decl sx_gum_call(u: node)
sx_gum_call(u) :- kind(u, "call"), field(u, "function", f), sym_of(f, q),
    (q = "django.contrib.auth.get_user_model" ; q = "django.contrib.auth.models.get_user_model").

// sx_user(mq): Meta.model mq is a user model with Django's `password` field: Django's own user classes, a run class
// deriving from one, `get_user_model()`, or another module's `User = get_user_model()` (mq is "<module>.User").
.decl sx_user_lib(q: symbol)
sx_user_lib("django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractUser"). sx_user_lib("django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractBaseUser").
sx_user_lib("django.contrib.auth.base_user.AbstractBaseUser"). sx_user_lib("django.contrib.auth.models.User").
.decl sx_user_alias(q: symbol)
sx_user_alias(q) :- modname(m, mod), rasg(m, x, r, _), unparen(r, u), sx_gum_call(u), q = cat(mod, ".", x).
.decl sx_user(mq: symbol)
sx_user("get_user_model()") :- sx_ser(_, "get_user_model()").
sx_user(mq) :- sx_ser(_, mq), sx_user_lib(mq).
sx_user(mq) :- sx_ser(_, mq), drf_cls_q(mq, k), drf_qbase(k, b), sx_user_lib(b).
sx_user(mq) :- sx_ser(_, mq), drf_cls_q(mq, k), drf_anc(k, a), drf_qbase(a, b), sx_user_lib(b).
sx_user(mq) :- sx_ser(_, mq), sx_user_alias(aq), (aq = mq ; suffix(cat(".", mq), aq)).

// sx_meta_mc(mc): model class mc of the run is some serializer's Meta.model: the only models whose fields are read.
.decl sx_meta_mc(mc: symbol)
sx_meta_mc(mc) :- sx_ser(_, mq), drf_cls_q(mq, mc).
// sx_body_field(q, x, t): class q's body assigns `x = <call>` with the callee's last name t ending in "Field": a model
// field class lib/django does not know too (the run's EncryptedTextField, a package's AESField). Stated in q's file.
.decl sx_body_field(q: symbol, x: symbol, t: symbol)
sx_body_field(q, x, t) :- drf_own_attr(c, x, v, _), unparen(v, k), kind(k, "call"), call_name(k, t), suffix("Field", t),
    class_def(c, q).
sx_body_field(q, x, t) :- dj_class_field(c, x, _, t), class_def(c, q).
// sx_model_field(mc, x, t): model mc has field x of class t, its own or a run base's (an abstract base, a mixin).
.decl sx_model_field(mc: symbol, x: symbol, t: symbol)
sx_model_field(mc, x, t) :- sx_meta_mc(mc), sx_body_field(mc, x, t).
sx_model_field(mc, x, t) :- sx_meta_mc(mc), drf_anc(mc, b), sx_body_field(b, x, t).

// sx_secret(mq, x): model mq has a field x holding a secret.
.decl sx_secret(mq: symbol, x: symbol)
sx_secret(mq, x) :- sx_ser(_, mq), drf_cls_q(mq, mc), sx_model_field(mc, x, t), sx_secret_name(x), !sx_plain_class(t).
sx_secret(mq, "password") :- sx_user(mq).

// sx_secret_name(x): the whole name x names a secret.
.decl sx_secret_name(x: symbol)
sx_secret_name(x) :- sx_model_field(_, x, _),
    (match("(?:.*_)?(?:password|passwd|passphrase)s?(?:_hash|_hashed|_digest)?", x) ;
     match("(?:.*_)?secrets?(?:_key|_access_key|_token|_value)?", x) ;
     match("(?:.*_)?token(?:_key|_secret|_value)?", x) ;
     match("(?:.*_)?tokens_(?:key|secret|value)", x) ;
     match("(?:.*_)?(?:api|secret|private|signing|encryption)_?keys?", x) ;
     match("(?:.*_)?(?:otp|totp|hotp)(?:_secret|_seed|_key)?", x) ;
     match("(?:.*_)?(?:mfa|2fa)_(?:secret|seed|key)", x) ;
     match("(?:.*_)?credentials?", x)).
// sx_plain_class(t): model field classes that cannot hold a secret.
.decl sx_plain_class(t: symbol)
sx_plain_class(t) :- sx_model_field(_, _, t), (suffix("IntegerField", t) ; suffix("AutoField", t) ; dj_relation_class(t) ;
    t = "BooleanField" ; t = "NullBooleanField" ; t = "DateTimeField" ; t = "DateField" ; t = "TimeField" ;
    t = "DurationField" ; t = "FloatField" ; t = "DecimalField").

// ---- what goes out -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// sx_out(c, mq, x, how, h, w): serializer c (model mq) returns secret field x, let in by Meta option h; w is the home
// whose value writes the listed string inside a class (the Meta, or a base's Meta), "" when the finding goes at h's
// value (`"__all__"`, `exclude`, or a string of a module constant).
.decl sx_out(c: symbol, mq: symbol, x: symbol, how: symbol, h: symbol, w: symbol)
sx_out(c, mq, x, "`fields = \"__all__\"` includes it", h, "") :- sx_ser(c, mq), sx_opt(c, "fields", h),
    drf_hstr(h, "__all__"), sx_secret(mq, x).
sx_out(c, mq, x, "`exclude` does not name it", h, "") :- sx_ser(c, mq), sx_opt(c, "exclude", h), sx_secret(mq, x),
    !drf_strs(h, x, _).
sx_out(c, mq, x, "`fields` lists it", h, w) :- sx_ser(c, mq), sx_opt(c, "fields", h), drf_strs(h, x, w),
    sx_secret(mq, x), !drf_hconst(w).
sx_out(c, mq, x, "`fields` lists it", h, "") :- sx_ser(c, mq), sx_opt(c, "fields", h), drf_strs(h, x, w),
    sx_secret(mq, x), drf_hconst(w).
// sx_str_spot(e, w, x): string node e, written in a class body, in home w's value, holds x.
.decl sx_str_spot(e: node, w: symbol, x: symbol)
sx_str_spot(e, w, x) :- drf_hv(w, v), drf_vlit_at(v, e, x), nearest(e, _, "class_definition").

// sx_method_out(c, mq, x, hd): serializer c (model mq) declares SerializerMethodField hd in its output (`fields`
// lists it, or is "__all__", or Meta uses `exclude`), whose method (`get_<name>`, or `method_name=`) returns
// `<obj>.x`, obj its instance parameter and x a secret field of mq. The method's body is read in its file
// (sx_returns_attr).
.decl sx_method_out(c: symbol, mq: symbol, x: symbol, hd: symbol)
sx_method_out(c, mq, x, hd) :- sx_ser(c, mq), drf_declared_q(c, f, o), hd = @dot(o, f),
    drf_decl_kind_q(hd, "SerializerMethodField"), sx_in_output(c, f), sx_method_name(hd, f, mn),
    drf_method_q(c, mn, fq), sx_returns_attr(fq, x), sx_secret(mq, x).
.decl sx_method_name(hd: symbol, f: symbol, mn: symbol)
sx_method_name(hd, f, mn) :- sx_smf(hd, f), drf_kw_q(hd, "method_name", hk), drf_hstr(hk, mn).
sx_method_name(hd, f, mn) :- sx_smf(hd, f), !sx_named_method(hd), mn = cat("get_", f).
.decl sx_smf(hd: symbol, f: symbol)
sx_smf(hd, f) :- sx_ser(c, _), drf_declared_q(c, f, o), hd = @dot(o, f), drf_decl_kind_q(hd, "SerializerMethodField").
.decl sx_named_method(hd: symbol)
sx_named_method(hd) :- drf_kw_q(hd, "method_name", _).
// sx_returns_attr(fq, x): method fq returns `<obj>.x`, obj its first parameter after self.
.decl sx_returns_attr(fq: symbol, x: symbol)
sx_returns_attr(fq, x) :- kind(fn, "function_definition"), params(fn, o, 1), kind(r, "return_statement"),
    def_frame(r, fn), child(r, e, 0), unparen(e, a), attr_of(a, on, x), kind(on, "identifier"), text(on, o),
    qualname(fn, fq).
.decl sx_in_output(c: symbol, f: symbol)
sx_in_output(c, f) :- sx_ser(c, _), drf_declared_q(c, f, _), sx_opt(c, "fields", h), drf_strs(h, f, _).
sx_in_output(c, f) :- sx_ser(c, _), drf_declared_q(c, f, _), sx_opt(c, "fields", h), drf_hstr(h, "__all__").
sx_in_output(c, f) :- sx_ser(c, _), drf_declared_q(c, f, _), sx_opt(c, "exclude", h), !drf_strs(h, f, _).

// ---- what hides it -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.decl sx_out_x(c: symbol, x: symbol)
sx_out_x(c, x) :- sx_out(c, _, x, _, _, _).
.decl sx_hidden(c: symbol, x: symbol)
// A declaration of x replaces the model field: hidden unless it is rest_framework's own field reading x for output.
sx_hidden(c, x) :- sx_out_x(c, x), sx_decl_value(c, x, h), !sx_decl_exposes(h, x).
sx_hidden(c, x) :- sx_out_x(c, x), drf_extra_kw_q(c, x, "write_only", t), drf_hkind(t, "true"), !sx_declares(c, x).
// A to_representation (own or a run base's) next to the name as a string in the class body or a run base's, outside
// a Meta: `data.pop("password")`, or a `secure_fields = ["password"]` list the method pops in a loop.
sx_hidden(c, x) :- sx_out_x(c, x), sx_to_rep(c), sx_body_str(c, x).
sx_hidden(c, x) :- sx_out_x(c, x), sx_to_rep(c), drf_anc(c, b), sx_body_str(b, x).
.decl sx_to_rep(c: symbol)
sx_to_rep(c) :- sx_ser(c, _), drf_qmethod(c, "to_representation", _).
sx_to_rep(c) :- sx_ser(c, _), drf_anc(c, b), drf_qmethod(b, "to_representation", _).
// sx_body_str(k, x): class k's own body (not a nested class's, such as its Meta) holds the string x, a name that may
// be a secret's (the exact names are sx_secret_name's).
.decl sx_body_str(k: symbol, x: symbol)
sx_body_str(k, x) :- str(n, x), match("(?i).*(pass|secret|token|key|otp|mfa|2fa|credential).*", x),
    nearest(n, kc, "class_definition"), class_def(kc, k).

// sx_decl_value(c, x, h): serializer c's attribute x is home h: its own `x = …`, else a run ancestor's.
.decl sx_decl_value(c: symbol, x: symbol, h: symbol)
sx_decl_value(c, x, h) :- sx_out_x(c, x), drf_qattr(c, x), h = @dot(c, x).
sx_decl_value(c, x, h) :- sx_out_x(c, x), drf_anc(c, b), drf_qattr(b, x), !drf_qattr(c, x), h = @dot(b, x).
.decl sx_declares(c: symbol, x: symbol)
sx_declares(c, x) :- sx_decl_value(c, x, _).
// sx_decl_exposes(h, x): the declaration is a rest_framework field, not HiddenField or SerializerMethodField, without
// write_only=True and without a `source=` naming another attribute.
.decl sx_decl_exposes(h: symbol, x: symbol)
sx_decl_exposes(h, x) :- sx_decl_value(_, x, h), drf_hcall(h, q), prefix("rest_framework.", q), split_dot(q, _, n),
    n != "HiddenField", n != "SerializerMethodField", !sx_write_only(h), !sx_other_source(h, x).
.decl sx_write_only(h: symbol)
sx_write_only(h) :- drf_kw_q(h, "write_only", hk), drf_hkind(hk, "true").
.decl sx_other_source(h: symbol, x: symbol)
sx_other_source(h, x) :- sx_decl_value(_, x, h), drf_kw_q(h, "source", hk), !drf_hstr(hk, x).

// The cases, `upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/`, read as one repository:
// each line ending in `# caught` is reported, and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "core/__init__.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/core/__init__.py"
    .fixture "core/fields.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/core/fields.py"
    .fixture "core/models.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/core/models.py"
    .fixture "accounts/__init__.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/accounts/__init__.py"
    .fixture "accounts/models.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/accounts/models.py"
    .fixture "accounts/serializers.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/accounts/serializers.py"
    .fixture "accounts/tests/__init__.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/accounts/tests/__init__.py"
    .fixture "accounts/tests/test_serializers.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/accounts/tests/test_serializers.py"
    .fixture "integrations/__init__.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/integrations/__init__.py"
    .fixture "integrations/models.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/integrations/models.py"
    .fixture "integrations/serializers.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/integrations/serializers.py"
    .fixture "backend/vault/__init__.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/backend/vault/__init__.py"
    .fixture "backend/vault/models.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/backend/vault/models.py"
    .fixture "backend/vault/api/__init__.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/backend/vault/api/__init__.py"
    .fixture "backend/vault/api/base.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/backend/vault/api/base.py"
    .fixture "backend/vault/api/serializers.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/backend/vault/api/serializers.py"
    .fixture "storage/__init__.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/storage/__init__.py"
    .fixture "storage/constants.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/storage/constants.py"
    .fixture "storage/models.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/storage/models.py"
    .fixture "storage/serializers.py" from "../upstream/drf-practice/authored/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/storage/serializers.py"
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":15
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":22
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":32
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":40
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":47
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":56
    .expect _ at "integrations/serializers.py":14
    .expect _ at "integrations/serializers.py":22
    .expect _ at "integrations/serializers.py":23
    .expect _ at "integrations/serializers.py":31
    .expect _ at "integrations/serializers.py":39
    .expect _ at "integrations/serializers.py":106
    .expect _ at "backend/vault/api/serializers.py":9
    .expect _ at "backend/vault/api/serializers.py":25
    .expect _ at "storage/serializers.py":16
    .expect _ at "storage/serializers.py":23
    .expect _ at "storage/serializers.py":30
    .expect _ at "storage/serializers.py":35
    .expect _ at "storage/serializers.py":47
    .expect _ at "storage/serializers.py":61
.end
